As shown in Equation (22), this product separates the electronic effects in $I_{t}\left( {eV}_{bias} - \hslash\omega \right)$ and the optical information in $D_{r}(\hslash\omega)$ with its validity for restricted to $\hslash\omega < {eV}_{bias} - O\left( k_{B}T \right)$. [32] $$I_{l}\left( \hslash\omega,V_{bias} \right) \propto \left\{ \begin{array}{r}                                                                                                                                  (22)
\begin{matrix}
D_{r}(\hslash\omega)\mathcal{R}_{inel}\left( \hslash\omega,V_{bias} \right) \cong D_{r}(\hslash\omega)I_{t}\left( {eV}_{bias} - \hslash\omega \right) & \hslash\omega < {eV}_{bias} - O\left( k_{B}T \right)
\end{matrix} \\
\begin{array}{r}
\  \\
\begin{matrix}
0 & \hslash\omega > {eV}_{bias} + O\left( k_{B}T \right)
\end{matrix}
\end{array}
\end{array} \right.\ $$

